            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac tamponade due to spontaneous rupture of large coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>422-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 70-year-old woman admitted with chest pain went into shock due to cardiac tamponade; 1000 mL of blood was drained from her pericardium. Enhanced computed tomography showed massive pericardial effusion and a coronary artery aneurysm in front of the main pulmonary artery. Coronary angiography revealed a coronary artery-pulmonary artery fistula and 3 giant saccular coronary artery aneurysms. Emergency surgical repair was successful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
